# Line endings — added at the v3.2.0 cut (umbrella #252; hazard named at #277/#279).
#
# This repo is PUBLIC and was committed from a machine with core.autocrlf=true and
# no .gitattributes. Every tracked file is LF in the index today (measured, 66/66),
# but nothing enforced it: a fresh Windows clone would materialise CRLF, and one
# commit from that clone could flip the whole tree. `text=auto` makes git normalise
# to LF in the index on commit regardless of the contributor's platform, so the
# index can no longer flip.
* text=auto

# Anything a POSIX shell executes is pinned to LF on checkout everywhere: a script
# whose lines end in \r fails on the far end with `$'\r': command not found`
# after the transfer succeeded (the droplet runs Ubuntu; umbrella #315 CRLF-keys).
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Never touch bytes in these.
*.db  binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
